# md2spa -> Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_redirects`
#
# Copy this file into the *output* directory (`static/_redirects` works: everything under
# staticDir is copied verbatim into outDir, so it lands next to index.html).
#
# Use this only if you are not using netlify.toml -- that file already carries the same
# rule, and mixing the two makes precedence hard to reason about.
#
# md2spa pre-renders every route to its own index.html, so static file serving already
# answers every real URL. This catch-all exists purely for genuine misses, and it must be
# the last rule: both Netlify and Cloudflare evaluate top to bottom, first match wins.
#
# Status 404 rather than 200 is deliberate. The generated 404.html re-derives the site
# base at runtime from its embedded route list, so it renders correctly at any depth --
# and a real miss should not be reported to crawlers as a success.

/*    /404.html   404
